WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.400
Requests rarely arrive as clear engineering tickets.

00:03.850 --> 00:10.500
They often begin as short messages with missing context,
unclear priorities, and uncertain expectations.

00:11.100 --> 00:16.050
Intake helps transform these requests into structured,
traceable work.

00:16.650 --> 00:21.900
Artificial intelligence reviews the original message,
identifies the key details, and proposes a practical next step.

00:22.500 --> 00:31.500
A person then checks the proposal, makes any necessary changes,
and decides whether it should be approved.

00:32.100 --> 00:37.850
Once approved, the work can be synchronized with GitHub
and included in the daily plan.

00:38.350 --> 00:44.400
The original request, the human decision,
and the delivery record remain connected.

00:44.900 --> 00:48.450
AI proposes.

00:49.000 --> 00:50.100
People decide.

00:50.450 --> 00:53.550
Every step stays traceable.
